{"kind":"assert","text":"RC-1 step 5: proposed class of every refusal reason, for your confirmation. Read at cutover head 411d2ecf. No build yet.\n\nCount: `REFUSAL_REASONS` (packages/bytes/src/records.ts:73-78) has 36 members at this head. `wrong-genesis` and `genesis-conflict` are not among them. `wrong-genesis` is a ReadRefusal, a RoutingRefusal and an Attempt answer (packages/contract/src/result.ts:55,65). `genesis-conflict` is the type CreationConflict (result.ts:71). The table covers RefusalReason only.\n\nnever (6):\n- archived: the floor only rises (derive/src/floor.ts:164). A kept set lists only positions still held (:173). An archived position stays archived.\n- floor-ahead: compares two numbers inside the input (floor.ts:167).\n- floor-back: `input.floor \u003c= current`, and current only rises (floor.ts:164).\n- floor-keep: shape checks of the bytes, plus `own(seq) === null` below the floor, which is archived (floor.ts:173).\n- scope-refused: status `refused` is set only at genesis (fold.ts:93). Only `activate` changes status (fold.ts:164-165), and confirm admits only a `provisional` scope (delivery.ts:321).\n- late: a refused delivery is written as a decision entry, and a later copy answers `repeat` (judge.ts:171). Source time plus bound stays before commit time.\n\nprotocol (5): misaddressed (address, judge.ts:223), unknown-act (judge.ts:246), unknown-message (delivery.ts:223), wrong-pin (delivery.ts:226), unsupported-definition (scope/src/core.ts:580,586).\n\nhead (25): floor-receipt, floor-step, floor-recent, floor-kept, revision-moved, alias, duplicate-relation, required-unset, scope-full, bad-intent, expired, bad-field, no-item, final, fact-mismatch, unauthorized, guard-failed, capability-refused, slot-full, type-full, entry-too-large, send-unresolved, application-revoked, limit, bad-input.\n\nThree differ from acf85bfa's reading, and each is `head` by your rule 4:\n1. revision-moved: the judge tests `expected !== item.revision` (judge.ts:312), not `\u003c`. Revisions rise by one per changing entry (fold.ts:199). Bytes whose `expected` is above the current revision can match later. `also` names that resolve by slot can bind another item later (handlers.ts:289-296).\n2. final: at judge.ts:316 the subject is `intent.on`, and a final state has no exit (fold.ts:125-126), so that site holds forever. The effects.ts sites (:274, :376) can name an `also` or computed item that resolves to another item later.\n3. expired: the judge checks `asOf \u003e= notAfter` (judge.ts:234), where `asOf = max(reading, last entry time)` (time.ts:28-29). A refusal writes no entry. If the reading goes back below notAfter and no entry is sealed in between, the same bytes are admitted.\n\nEach of the three becomes `never` with a change to the judge: refuse revision-moved only when `expected \u003c revision` on a fixed id, split final by subject, or record the refusal time for expired. That changes answers, which RC-1 excludes, so I propose `head` and no change.\n\nbad-intent and bad-field mix failures of the bytes alone with failures of clock or context. Splitting them would make most cases `never`. Not proposed for RC-1.\n\nThe table goes beside REFUSAL_REASONS in packages/bytes/src/records.ts. I will check docs/kernel.md section 7 for that file before the build and say so in the note."}